albumin corrected anion gap (in mEq/L) = sodium (mEq/L) - (chloride (mEq/L) + bicarbonate (mEq/L));
albumin corrected anion gap (in mEq/L) = 125.0 mmol/L (Na) - (87.0 mmol/L (Cl) + 28.0 mmol/L (HCO3));
albumin corrected anion gap (in mEq/L) = 125 - 87 - 28 = 20; Δ anion gap (in mEq/L) = albumin corrected anion gap - 12;
Δ anion gap (in mEq/L) = 20 - 12 = 8; Delta albumin (in mEq/L) = Δ anion gap - albumin.
